    "body": "## Principal continuation\n\nReferences #820, #973. Broad language, memory, coding, energy and release responsibilities remain open.\n\n### Implemented workstreams\n- Sparse integer IPL1 prior and PRC2 model-plus-prior bundle, marginal-relative correction, Generate-group mass preservation and measured Copy/Stop behavior.\n- Full 114,364-target Tune adjudication, local/history/reversal controls, rare-tail accounting, interpolation recheck and lag1–4 transport probes.\n- Exact served-weight warm initialization with fresh optimizer state, two schedules and two shuffle seeds, byte-identical fresh-process replay, and grounded retention checks.\n- Four source-family evaluations frozen before download, actual generation, same-loaded-composite grounding and interleaved cost measurements.\n- Finite Hamilton/Q8 vector actions with inverse, norm, sign, order and common-rotation tests. This is not a learned-attention qualification.\n\n### Results\nThe first decaying warm candidate improves 7.03268 to **6.27371 bits/target**, retaining temporal32/32, training36/36, class4/4 and held-out3/3. A second shuffle seed confirms the recipe. Both constant-rate candidates lose one held-out example and are preserved negatives.\n\nThe integer marginal-relative readout scores **5.03801** on the original prose artifact. Frozen coefficients transferred to the warm model score **5.01774** with authored grounding retained. The raw product harms rare tokens; the ratio family improves both stratum point estimates. A retuned reversed-history ratio ties full history, so no unique chronological-order or geometric advantage is claimed.\n\nThe frozen ratio and warm native model improve their respective baselines in all four external books. Absolute loss remains poor and generation remains repetitive. Isolated native emitted-token feedback still fails its crossed test. Full scoped-session and composite crossed-feedback qualification remain open. The later warm-composite book evaluation is explicitly an exposed-source follow-up.\n\n### Verification and preservation\n- **49 focused tests rerun:** integer prior/ratio7, Hamilton6, transferable lexical13, runner23. Not a full repository suite.\n- Native verification of19 sealed experiment reports and the retained candidate root;429 pinned corpus hashes verified.\n- Exact warm replay and transferred-bundle replay; Q12 mass identity and maximum per-target realization difference below0.000418bits.\n- Rust code diff unchanged by rebase onto owner-direction PR#1370. Original experiment source retained on `archive/principal-evidence-source-20260923`.\n- Debug output and redundant checkouts reclaimed only after unique uncommitted files were archived and hash-verified. Cleanup reached55.10GB free; the final measured space and resource checkpoint are recorded. Owner tracked edits remain unchanged; one live .omo continuation record changed during the session and is disclosed.\n\n### Delivery boundary\nNo default serving artifact or Studio/API model is silently replaced. The principal handoff binds retained artifacts and restart paths. The endpoint remains fully transformerless geometric language modeling with geometry replacing floating-point matrix multiplication, not a table-only output architecture.\n\nThe historical CI status names acknowledge compatibility, not test execution. Local executed checks supply validation. Deliver through the normal protected merge queue.\n",
